INT. NIGHTBIRD STUDIOS - LIVE ROOM - NIGHT

Midnight. Rain on the roof.

HISS of the tape machine. A red RECORD light.

Foam panels. Cables like veins. A grand piano under a sheet.

RILEY, 30s, producer, hunches over the console. He rubs his eyes. Coffee gone cold.

Behind the glass, PRIYA, 20s, singer, stands at the mic. Headphones on. Eyes closed.

COLE, 40s, engineer, slouches by the patch bay. He chews a pen.

RILEY
(into talkback)
Take eleven. From the bridge.

PRIYA
(through speaker)
Can I hear the guide?

RILEY
It's in your cans.

PRIYA
It's not.

He checks the fader. Pushes it up.

BZZZT. Feedback.

Everyone flinches.

COLE
That wasn't me.

RILEY
Mute the room mics.

COLE
They're muted.

Silence.

Then a soft sound in the speakers. A breath.

Not Priya's.

PRIYA
(through speaker)
Riley? Who's in here with me?

RILEY
Nobody. It's the monitors.

He taps the glass. She doesn't turn.

PHONE BUZZES on the console. He grabs it.

ON PHONE: where r u

ON PHONE: the door is open

He frowns. Looks at the live room door. Shut. Locked. Light off.

COLE
Who is it?

RILEY
Dez. He's not even in the building.

He thumbs a call. Puts it on speaker.

RING. RING.

DEZ (V.O.)
(distorted, far)
Riley? Why are you calling from my house?

RILEY
What? I'm at the studio.

DEZ (V.O.)
I'm at the studio. I'm in the live room. Priya's with me.

Beat.

Riley looks through the glass.

Priya is alone. Mouth open. Singing. No sound.

COLE
Kill the tape.

RILEY
I'm trying.

COLE
Kill it!

RILEY
It's not responding!

BANG.

The piano sheet FLIES off.

The keys PLUNGE. Alone.

A chord. Low. Wrong.

PRIYA
(through speaker)
It knows my name.

RILEY
Priya, come out. Now.

PRIYA
(through speaker)
It's saying it.

COLE
Saying what?

DEZ (V.O.)
Don't open the door.

RILEY
Dez, where are you?

DEZ (V.O.)
Don't open the door don't open the door--

CLICK. Dead line.

A dog BARKS outside. Frantic. A delivery kid on the sidewalk ducks under an awning, phone raised, filming the building. The dog drags its leash toward the street.

Inside, the lights DIE.

Red RECORD light only.

COLE
Where's the exit?

RILEY
Behind you.

COLE
There's a wall behind me!

PRIYA
(through speaker)
Riley. Riley. Riley.

RILEY
I'm coming.

COLE
Don't.

RILEY
She's in there!

COLE
She's not alone!

The glass CRACKS. A line zigzags across it.

Priya turns. Slowly.

Her eyes are open. They aren't hers.

PRIYA
(her voice, doubled)
Take twelve.

The speakers SCREAM.

Every fader slams to the top.

Riley grabs the door. It burns.

He kicks it. SLAM. It gives.

He drags Cole through. They hit the corridor running.

The red light follows them. Down the hall. Faster.

BOOM.

The whole building exhales.

EXT. NIGHTBIRD STUDIOS - STREET - CONTINUOUS

They tumble out into the rain.

Behind them, the windows blow out in a shower of light.

Silence.

Riley's phone BUZZES.

ON PHONE: take twelve

He drops it into a puddle.
